[00:15.57] I'm not one to look behind
[00:18.56] I know that times must change
[00:22.83] But over there in Barrytown
[00:26.20] They do things very strange
[00:30.28] And though you're not my enemy
[00:34.15] I like things like they used to be
[00:38.12] And though you'd like some company
[00:41.36] I'm standing by myself
[00:45.24] Go play with someone else
[00:49.28] I can see by what you carry
[00:52.48] That you come from Barrytown
[01:03.10] Don't believe I'm taken in
[01:06.17] By stories I have heard
[01:10.70] I just read the Daily News
[01:13.85] And swear by every word
[01:18.04] And don't think that I'm out of line
[01:22.00] For speaking out for what is mine
